  "_comment": [
    "SYNTHETIC — hand-built from the documented response shapes in Yahoo's official",
    "Fantasy Sports API guide and from published wrapper-library samples (yfpy,",
    "yahoo_fantasy_api). NOT a live capture. Yahoo API access is gated behind an",
    "approval application and NO live call has ever been made from this repo.",
    "Replace with a real redacted capture once API access is approved.",
    "",
    "AUTHORED 2026-08-11 (not captured on any date). The 32 player resources were",
    "hand-authored and then serialized by a throwaway script so that every one of",
    "them has the identical field ORDER and nesting — a hand-typed 25-entry page",
    "would eventually contain a typo that looked exactly like a parser bug.",
    "",
    "REDACTION: league and team identifiers are invented; headshot URLs are fake",
    "(FAKEHEADSHOT<id>). Player names are real NFL players — public sports data,",
    "not personal data of any league member — and their numeric ids are PLAUSIBLE",
    "BUT UNVERIFIED. No token, email or real GUID appears anywhere here.",
    "",
    "MODELS: GET /fantasy/v2/league/461.l.576919/players;start=25;count=25?format=json",
    "",
    "WHY THIS IS COMMITTED — THIS IS THE SHORT PAGE, AND 'SHORT' MEANS STOP.",
    "7 items came back from a request for 25, so this is the last page and",
    "pagination terminates here. yahoo_players_page1.json is the other half of",
    "the rule: full page → keep going, short page → stop. Get that backwards in",
    "either direction and you either burn 40 requests per league on nothing or",
    "silently ingest a fraction of the player universe while every row you did",
    "get looks perfectly valid.",
    "",
    "SHAPE HAZARDS DELIBERATELY PRESENT:",
    "  1. 'players' is a numeric-key COLLECTION with a sibling 'count' of 7 —",
    "     the provider's own declared count, which a caller should compare",
    "     against the number of rows actually parsed. A mismatch is what a",
    "     truncated read looks like from the outside.",
    "  2. Marquez Valdes-Scantling is a FREE AGENT: editorial_team_abbr 'FA' with",
    "     an EMPTY-STRING editorial_team_key and editorial_team_full_name. Empty",
    "     is Yahoo saying 'no team'; absent would mean 'not returned'. Those are",
    "     different claims and to_text() preserves '' deliberately.",
    "  3. He also has NO bye week — an unrostered player has no bye — so the",
    "     bye_weeks key is absent entirely rather than 0.",
    "  4. Same double-nested player resource and single-element eligible_positions",
    "     collapse as page 1.",
    "",
    "NOT TRUNCATED — the count of 7 IS the fixture."
